# CQ 01: Which AI systems does a model contain, and which components make up
# each?
#
# 3.1.4 defines the AI system as an engineered system generating outputs for a
# given set of human-defined objectives, 3.1.2 the component as a functional
# element constructing it.
#
# A system without components is not an error. Cases 1 and 2 relate their
# functions to the system directly, which suffices while there is one of each
# kind. Case 3 needs the components, since two of them perform the same kind of
# function differently.
PREFIX iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/instances#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#>
SELECT ?system (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?c; separator=", ") AS ?components)
WHERE {
  ?system a iso:AISystem .
  OPTIONAL { ?system iso:consistsOf ?component }
  BIND(COALESCE(STR(?component), "") AS ?c)
} GROUP BY ?system ORDER BY ?system
